    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d845">

                <pb facs="0830" n="726" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg726"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/6302.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at
                            Saltillo to the Secretary of
                        State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Saltillo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-21T13:00:00-06:41">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 21, 1913—1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Governor Carranza has officially announced to me that he will conform with the
                    new administration at Mexico City. All opposition here abandoned. Railroads will
                    be opened at once. Perfect quiet prevails.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Holland</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
